# AnnW LanMp — Architecture Gate

When working under `LanMp/` or `docs/lan-mp/`:

## Non-negotiable (ADR-004 / INV-T*)

1. **Turn cursor** (`turns`, `current_co_index`, `cur_player`) advances on Host only via vanilla turn code; Guest applies **only** through `EndTurn` Command fields (`nextPlayerIndex`, `turnsAfter`).
2. **Never** fix desync by adding another Harmony `Prefix` that calls `MannualEndTurn` on Guest to "catch up".
3. All battle `Command` applies go through **`CommandApplyQueue`** (serial). No parallel `CoApply*`.
4. Non-local seats (remote human + all AI) use **one** RemoteWatch path.
5. LAN: do not let `last_human_player.defeated` alone stop the global turn loop.
6. MatchEnd is Host-only and multi-seat; no single-bool fake settlement as the design.
7. **INV-SOLO (red line):** Installing LanMp must not change solo / campaign / vanilla skirmish battle semantics. Harmony may stay patched, but every Prefix/Postfix/Transpiler helper that can mutate behavior must **no-op or match vanilla exactly** unless `InLanBattle`+`GatesArmed` (battle) or explicit LAN lobby context (`LanRoomPanel` / `StartAuthorized` / seat seed). Documented leaks that were fixed: nested `TriggerFOWDirty` **body** block (solo+LAN), `UI_SkillBtn` energy_max rewrite, `CanDoAction` FOW rewrite to owner/cur_player, CoSelect free-PS unlock for all skirmish, stuck `PresentationSkipActionCell` / `SuppressNetworkEmit` after leave.
8. **INV-VIEW:** In LAN, `last_human_player` means **local FOW/UI viewer**, never the remote human whose turn it is. Do not let vanilla hotseat assignment fight FOWDirty rebinding (main-thread FOW re-entry freeze on Host EndTurn→Guest). **Never block nested `TriggerFOWDirty` bodies** (CO skills nest FOW during cast — same class of break as INV-SOLO). LAN-only: call `ApplyLocalViewBinding` on the **outermost** FOWDirty entry only. Unbound CO `CanDoAction`/`GetEffectZone` FOW must stay **caster `action.player`**, never local spectator FOW (Host Accept Guest cast / Guest presenting remote cast).
9. Host authoritative EndTurn Accept uses **`SuppressNetworkEmit` only** — never `ApplyingRemoteCommand` (that flag is Guest/replay).
10. **CoroutineObject ≠ Unity:** `yield return null` on `GameController` busy-spins the same `ExecuteContext` (Host EndTurn white-screen / Guest Apply stuck / Host AI freeze). Waits must use `AnnWCoroutine.NextTick` (`0f`). **CommandApplyQueue / Host Accept / Host turn progression (`EndPlayerTurn`/`StartNextPlayerTurn`) must drive bodies through `AnnWCoroutine.SafePump`** (flatten nested `IEnumerator`, map null/`0`/`0f`→NextTick) — never `yield return` vanilla animators straight into CoroutineObject. **Dual timeout:** (a) **Hang budget** — Apply/HostAccept anim SafePump 45s, skill CastDone 45s, Guest Intent await soft/hard — stuck animator / lost Nack. (b) **Turn-span** — Host turn/AI SafePump `NoTimeout`, Guest RemoteWatch until EndTurn/battle-leave (no 600s), Host EndTurn Accept wait for `EndTurnReady` unbounded — human AFK and multi-AI are valid silence; dead TCP is Net heartbeat. **`SuppressNetworkEmit` must not span turn-span waits** — use `HostEndTurnAcceptWaiting` so Bus UnitMoved/DoAction still emit during StartPlayerTurn prologue / AI; MannualEndTurn entry only needs a short Suppress. Boxed `int 0` (vanilla move/attack lerp) must yield one tick — treating it as wait-0s teleports Guest units.
11. **Checksum:** LAN checkpoints are EndTurn `stateHash` over the **attachment payload**. Recapture/`Save_General` drift after Apply must not Strict-pause Guest (Apply is lossy; Host attachment is ADR-001 truth).
12. **Guest Intent in-flight:** Guest may have at most one mutating Intent awaiting Host Command/Nack. No click-spam Accept. Host Accept must `SuppressNetworkEmit` through `HostBroadcastCommand` so Bus cannot emit a twin Command.
13. **INV-ACCEPT:** Board geometry/FOW legality for Guest UnitMoved/DoAction is **Host Accept only** (`ActionLegality` / `IntentAcceptLegalityRules`). Guest gate may block ownership/spent/spectate/in-flight — **never** fail-fast `GetMoveZone`/`CanDoAction` (0.18.2 regression). Host move: `GetMoveZone(false,true,false)` hard miss; DoAction: hard `IsPosInSelectZone` + hard `CanDoAction` FOW under **PreferUnitOwnerFow** (`TARGET_NOT_VISIBLE` / DETECTED≠SEEN — no soft-pass). Guest UX: INV-VIEW transpile + post-attach `RefreshLocalVision` (vision + combat UX caches). Always bind Intent extras before CanDoAction.
14. **Seat defeat / Surrender:** `player.defeated` stamps from attachment **independent of eco ResourceApplyMode** (`ApplySeatDefeatFlags` + `TriggerPlayerDefeat`). Surrender ≠ EndGame; MatchEnd settlement uses vanilla `proc_EndGame` (`AllowVanillaEndGameUi`), never custom IMGUI. **LAN `CheckSkirmishEndGame`:** settle only when ≤1 living non-neutral faction remains — never because "no Human controller left" (vanilla hotseat); allied AI / other seats keep the match so the surrendering peer spectates. **LAN Surrender Prefix must never `return true`** to vanilla `Surrender` (`EndGame(false)`) — including under `SuppressNetworkEmit` — or Host surrender instantly settles while allied humans still fight.
15. **CastSkill presentation:** Guest must **not** run vanilla `DoActionAni` (PrepareAction `AutoSetPos().Value` + MultiTarget sibling `CoroutineObject.StartCoroutine` → NRE / soft-lock). Guest: safe VFX + attach-only. Host Accept/local: SafePump `proc_SkillDoAction`; LAN `CoroutineObject.StartCoroutine` under skill/apply flags wraps SafePump (INV-T10). Host Command must carry `hasTarget`/tile/extras — never default aim (0,0). Ownership skills need `ownerIndex`→`ConvertUnitOwnerShip` (LoadOb does not OnEffectStart).
16. **MatchEnd settlement attachment:** Host `BroadcastMatchEnd` must capture `PlayerBattleStatics` + `turn_snaps` into `MatchEndPayload.settlementJson`; both peers stamp via `MatchSettlementBridge` **before** `AllowVanillaEndGameUi`→`EndGame`. Guest never accumulates statics/snaps (no Die / no NextTurn) — empty local ledgers → PageStat zeros / broken history. After MatchEnd: **leave room** (full Disconnect, not KeepHosting), **never** reopen `LanRoomPanel`/`LanLobby*` over MissionEnd/LevelSummary; `MatchSettled` disconnect must not toast「主机已离开」or reopen lobby.
17. **INV-UX-FALLTHROUGH:** LAN Intent-capture Prefixes must classify `return true` under Suppress/Applying:
    - **Allow** only when Accept/Apply is driving *this* method (`MannualEndTurn` Accept entry, Undo under `ApplyingRemoteCommand`, skill under `SkillCastSuppressEmit`).
    - **Never** for destructive hotseat (`Surrender`→`EndGame(false)`, `RestartLevel`) — always LAN body / block.
    - **Block** (toast) player UX under Suppress owned by a *different* command (undo/skill during UnitMoved Accept) — do not unsynced mutate while Bus is silenced.
    - `ShouldBlockUx` must not spectate-block Host Accept CastSkill (`SkillCastSuppressEmit` while remote seat is `cur_player`).
    - Quit notify (`NotifyLeavingBattle`) must run even under Suppress/Applying. No peers after Apply ≠ `broadcast-failed` Abort (Bus skip / CastSkill done).

## Process

- Architectural failures (split operators, double EndTurn, Host-defeat kills match) → change `TurnAuthority` / `CommandApplyQueue` / MatchEnd — **not** a one-off Prefix.
- Feature work (Guest AutoCmd, etc.) waits until P0 turn authority acceptance criteria pass.
- Declare which INV-T* a change upholds in the PR/commit message or reply.
